'''Tet'niss''', also known as the '''Mama Crab''',<ref name="Tippett Studio" /> was a gigantic [[Gender|female]] [[trash crab]] on [[Lanupa]].<ref name="Zero Friends Again" />

{{Species-stub}}

==Behind the scenes==
Tet'niss, albeit unidentified, first appeared in "[[Zero Friends Again]]," the sixth episode of the [[Disney+]] series ''[[Star Wars: Skeleton Crew]]'',<ref name="Zero Friends Again" /> which aired on [[December 31]], [[2024]].<ref name="Release">{{Twitter|StarWars|status/1861409832349172011|[[Star Wars]]|quote=Mark your calendars. 🗓️ On December 2, stream the two-episode series premiere of #SkeletonCrew, only on @DisneyPlus.|archiveurl=https://archive.ph/QwMYe}}</ref> The creature was achieved in the episode using mostly stop-motion animation produced by [[Tippett Studio]]. During production, the giant trash crab was nicknamed "Tet'niss" by the animators,<ref name="Guide">{{SW|url=series/skeleton-crew/season-1-episode-6-episode-guide|text="Zero Friends Again" Episode Guide &#124; Star Wars: Skeleton Crew}}</ref> which was later used as her [[in-universe]] name. She was also given the scientific name ''Megapagurus detritiphorus'', which means "big hermit crab carrying trash".<ref name="Tippett Studio" />

